# mneme environment variables — reference documentation
#
# Neither the CLI nor the MCP server auto-loads a .env file.
# Set these variables in the process environment directly:
#
#   Shell (add to ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc for persistence):
#     export MNEME_DB_PATH=/custom/path/memory.sqlite
#
#   MCP host config (Claude Desktop, VS Code, etc.):
#     { "env": { "MNEME_DB_PATH": "/custom/path/memory.sqlite" } }
#
# All variables are optional — mneme works without any configuration.

# Override the SQLite database file path.
# If not set, mneme uses the platform-standard data directory:
#   Linux:   ~/.local/share/mneme/memory.sqlite
#   macOS:   ~/Library/Application Support/mneme/memory.sqlite
#   Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\mneme\memory.sqlite
#
# A relative path is resolved against the current working directory
# of the process at startup.
# MNEME_DB_PATH=/custom/path/to/memory.sqlite
